  "verbalization": "Doxorubicin is linked to C2BBe1 through a series of molecular interactions, with the most direct pathway involving the compound [(1R)-1-[(5Z)-4-Bromo-5-(Bromomethylidene)-2-Oxofuran-3-Yl]Butyl] Acetate. This compound is both a target of doxorubicin and a target of palmarumycin CP18, which in turn targets C2BBe1. The evidence suggests that doxorubicin may act through a mechanism that indirectly affects C2BBe1 by first engaging with a common intermediate, [(1R)-1-[(5Z)-4-Bromo-5-(Bromomethylidene)-2-Oxofuran-3-Yl]Butyl] Acetate, which is shared as a target by both doxorubicin and palmarumycin CP18. This shared target implies a potential mechanism of action where doxorubicin may influence C2BBe1 through a common biochemical pathway, possibly involving receptor activation or enzyme inhibition. The evidence supports a model where doxorubicin and palmarumycin CP18 act on a shared target, C2BBe1, through a common intermediate, thereby linking the two entities in a molecular network.",
